flowchart TB
    accTitle: Extending the generic client engine
    accDescr: Four variants plug into the same engine. Hexa Quest illustrates the domain and presentation extension points and the two registrations that connect a fifth variant.

    Merge["Hexa Merge"] --> Engine
    Sort["Hexa Sort"] --> Engine
    Engine["Generic engine · GameEngine and Board<br/>Variants supply cell, move and state types<br/>and rules through IGameRules"]
    Fit["Hexa Fit"] --> Engine
    Lines["Hexa Lines"] --> Engine

    Engine -.- Quest["Hexa Quest · proposed fifth variant"]
    Quest -.-> Domain["Domain · layer 1<br/>Cell, move, state and IGameRules implementation<br/>BaseGameRules or SourcedGameRules<br/>IVariantFactory creates a session and progress model"]
    Quest -.-> Presentation["Presentation · layer 3<br/>VariantPresentationFactory supplies<br/>ICellRenderer and IInputMapper"]

    Domain -->|"domain factory registration"| Wiring
    Presentation -->|"presentation factory registration"| Wiring
    Wiring["Composition root · layer 4<br/>VariantFactoryRegistry + VariantPresentationRegistry<br/>Register both factories under the same gameId"]
    Domain --- Options["Additional domain extension points<br/>IScoringPolicy · IPieceSource · IProgressModel<br/>LevelSpec and ILevelValidator for level-based variants<br/>IUndoable for variants with undo"]

